## 📋 Architectural Plan — Vendor Invoice Processing

### Summary
A Maestro flow that accepts a vendor invoice PDF, extracts structured fields (invoice number, vendor name, date, total, line items) using your trained IxP model, and returns the extracted data as flow outputs. Error handling ensures the flow completes cleanly even if extraction fails.

### Flow Diagram

```mermaid
graph LR
    start(Receive Invoice)
    extractInvoice[Extract Invoice Fields]
    formatResults[Format Extracted Fields]
    handleError[Handle Extraction Error]
    doneSuccess(Done)
    doneError(Done Error)
    start -->|output| extractInvoice
    extractInvoice -->|output| formatResults
    extractInvoice -->|error| handleError
    formatResults -->|output| doneSuccess
    handleError -->|output| doneError
```

### Node Table

| # | Node ID | Name | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `start` | Receive Invoice | `core.trigger.manual` | Flow input: `invoiceFileRef` (string) — the PDF to process |
| 2 | `extractInvoice` | Extract Invoice Fields | `core.logic.mock` | **Placeholder** for your Vendor Invoices IxP model. Swap in once deployed to a folder |
| 3 | `formatResults` | Format Extracted Fields | `core.action.script` | Pulls Invoice Number, Vendor Name, Date, Total Amount, Line Items from IxP output |
| 4 | `handleError` | Handle Extraction Error | `core.action.script` | Captures error details for the error path |
| 5 | `doneSuccess` | Done | `core.control.end` | Outputs extracted fields |
| 6 | `doneError` | Done Error | `core.control.end` | Outputs error message |

### Flow Inputs / Outputs

| Direction | Name | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `in` | `invoiceFileRef` | string | File reference for the PDF invoice to process |
| `out` | `invoiceNumber` | string | Extracted invoice number |
| `out` | `vendorName` | string | Extracted vendor name |
| `out` | `invoiceDate` | string | Extracted invoice date |
| `out` | `totalAmount` | string | Extracted total amount |
| `out` | `lineItems` | string | Extracted line items (JSON string) |
| `out` | `errorMessage` | string | Error details if extraction fails |

