=== AGENT (turn 7) — 20.0s, in=4 out=755, 1 tool calls ===
There are three SAP connectors available. I need to understand which one you're using before I can check for a connection. They're quite different:

| Connector | What it's for |
|---|---|
| **SAP BAPI/RFC** (`uipath-sap-bapi`) | Calls SAP function modules directly (BAPIs, RFCs) — the classic way to create vendor invoices in ECC/S4 |
| **SAP OData** (`uipath-sap-odata`) | REST-style API calls to SAP S/4HANA — modern approach for S/4 |
| **SAP C4C** (`uipath-sap-c4cv2`) | SAP Cloud for Customer (CRM) — not for invoice accounting |
| **SAP Concur** (`uipath-sap-concur`) | Concur expense/travel — not for AP invoices |

The two realistic options for posting vendor invoices are **BAPI/RFC** (SAP ECC or older S/4HANA) and **OData** (S/4HANA Cloud or newer S/4). 

Which SAP system do you have — is it **ECC**, **S/4HANA**, or do you know if your team uses terms like "BAPI" or "OData" when talking about SAP integrations?

